// User account creation (persistence indicator)
//
// New local accounts are a common persistence technique. useradd writes a
// "new user:" line describing the account (name, UID, GID, home, shell).
//
// When the account is created through sudo, this also correlates with the
// matching sudo COMMAND line from privilege-escalation.kql at the same
// timestamp, showing who created the account and how.

Syslog
| where SyslogMessage has_any ("useradd", "new user")
| project TimeGenerated, Computer, ProcessName, SyslogMessage
| order by TimeGenerated desc
